Z||000003||Songman||10-05-2000||12:56 AM||||Well, from the point of view I have as an old man (35!) that has been through all of this stuff, let me say just one thing.... It don't get no better! They don't grow out of it!<P>I don't know your ages and I only know what you told us of the story but it seems obvious that you still care about her and it sounds like she still cares about you. If you do still care about her, I say go for it. Tell her that you still care and that you like the way you are when the two of you are together. The worst that can happen is that she will say no... or even worse, she can say yes and you will have to spend the rest of your life with her. Just kidding about that last part.<P>Women are a pain in the ass, there is no doubt... But has anyone found anything better for snuggling up with? I don't think so... and some of them can even cook! Good luck to you, my friend...||||reg||3
Z||000004||Gold-86SE||10-05-2000||09:15 AM||||<BR>Formula, I usually don't say anything with personal threads, but this one I think I have some advice.  After reading this, it is my observation from what you stated that there is a communication breakdown between the two of you.<P>Women (at least from what my wife, of going on 9 years, has told me) want you to talk with them.  My wife and I have a fairly decent communications forum.  Sure, some times we yell and fight, but the making up is fun.  I suggest that you bridge the gap and speak to her regarding the situation you find yourselves.  If you cannot speak with her and work out a solution, I say move on to a better catch.  Problems will always arise in a relationship whether bf/gf or husband/wife.  If a relationship is going to last and have strength against the challenges of life, you must communicate with one another.<P>Best of luck.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.txconnect.com/home/rharris/signature-a.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||RiceCooker||10-05-2000||02:20 PM||||Gold86SE's right. It's all about communication, I've learned this not only from my own experiences but from my parents' relationships, divorces, etc.<BR>It's actually worked out because i learned from their mistakes and right now i'm in the perfect relationship that i do believe will last forever (sniff, sniff)<BR>Seriously though, me and my girlfriend can and do talk about everything.<BR>Good luck||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||10-05-2000||04:11 PM||||I agree with My7Fieros..My X wife was always unhappy for what she didn't have.  Got  a house built...whine.. well it would be better if were built over in X town. Got a new car  whine.. well it could have been a Cadallac.  Go on vacation to Florida  whine.. I wanted to go to Europe.  When she left for better opportunities it cost me a lot. I was free and her better opportunity split, after a couple of years.  I haven't heard from her in sixteen years.<P>My Fieros have been more reliable.  When I'm ready to go, they are ready.  When I want them turned on, I stick a key into it and it gets turned on.  If one doesn't start I take the other on.  My 87 isn't jealous of my 88.  No matter what I spend on the car, it was less than I would have had to spend on that woman. Being married was the biggest cash drain on my life.  If you found a good one, I think that is the exception.<P>What's on TV?||||reg||5
Z||000007||Tigger||10-05-2000||05:33 PM||||I'd say if the two of you are really good friends and know each other well and like each other, then maybe you could try to work things out.  The gift sounds like it a very nice thing, she probably had a tough time accepting it because maybe she's not sure she can't afford a gift that $$$ for you in return.  These things are not always easy sometimes.  Like these guys have said, keep the communication going and hope things work out for ya.<P>After reading Old Lar's post, I don't know what my Fiero would think if I brought another one home?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">          <BR> <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
